WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:02.968
-Our next guest is
a Tony-nominated actor

00:00:02.968 --> 00:00:05.133
you know from shows like
"Spin City," "Mad About You,"

00:00:05.133 --> 00:00:07.968
and "Curb Your Enthusiasm," as
well as the movie "Inside Out."

00:00:07.968 --> 00:00:09.901
He stars in "East New York,"

00:00:09.901 --> 00:00:11.801
which airs Sunday nights
on CBS

00:00:11.801 --> 00:00:13.234
and streams on Paramount Plus.

00:00:13.234 --> 00:00:14.234
Let's take a look.

00:00:14.234 --> 00:00:15.267
-I believe in what you're doing.

00:00:15.267 --> 00:00:17.000
I understand why
you're doing it.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.467
I'm just afraid that the forces
arrayed against you

00:00:19.467 --> 00:00:21.133
may be overwhelming.

00:00:21.133 --> 00:00:23.734
-I expect to have the support
of Chief Suarez.

00:00:23.734 --> 00:00:26.601
If it's politically advangeous,
I expect to have the support

00:00:26.601 --> 00:00:28.100
of Deputy Mayor Sharpe.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:30.634
I also just might

00:00:30.634 --> 00:00:34.601
have the support of the people
who live in East New York.

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:36.934
-And you have me.

00:00:36.934 --> 00:00:38.534
-Please welcome back
to the show,

00:00:38.534 --> 00:00:40.868
the one, the only Richard Kind!

00:00:40.868 --> 00:00:44.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:44.033 --> 00:00:51.868
♪♪

00:00:51.868 --> 00:00:58.968
♪♪

00:00:58.968 --> 00:01:06.701
♪♪

00:01:06.701 --> 00:01:10.968
♪♪

00:01:10.968 --> 00:01:13.400
-Let's get rid of this, 'cause
I want to just talk to you

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:15.534
and not worry about
anybody who's calling.

00:01:15.534 --> 00:01:16.667
I just want to talk to you.
-Okay, thank you.

00:01:16.667 --> 00:01:17.934
-'Cause we're on TV.

00:01:17.934 --> 00:01:19.200
-You do use the compass app,
though.

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:21.968
-All the time!
And Google Maps all the time.

00:01:21.968 --> 00:01:23.601
You get out of a subway,

00:01:23.601 --> 00:01:24.667
you don't know which way
you're going.

00:01:24.667 --> 00:01:27.234
Where's Sullivan Street?
Is it north?

00:01:27.234 --> 00:01:29.234
[ Applause ]
Thank you!

00:01:29.234 --> 00:01:31.133
I'm a man of the people.

00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:32.400
-Oh, boy.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:34.734
Right off the bat. Right off
the bat with the pander.

00:01:34.734 --> 00:01:35.868
Congratulations!

00:01:35.868 --> 00:01:37.167
You have played so many
different roles

00:01:37.167 --> 00:01:39.200
over your career, and here you
are as a police officer.

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:40.667
-I'm a cop.
-Wow.

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:43.167
-I'm a New York cop.
-Look at you.

00:01:43.167 --> 00:01:45.067
-It's unbelievable,
and when I got hired --

00:01:45.067 --> 00:01:48.334
my resume is, like you said,

00:01:48.334 --> 00:01:50.634
"Inside Out" and "Curb"
and comedies,

00:01:50.634 --> 00:01:52.467
and then look at what
I look like.

00:01:52.467 --> 00:01:54.868
-Yeah.
-And I walk down the street

00:01:54.868 --> 00:01:56.300
and I see some of the
New York cops

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:59.834
with stomachs here and I go,
"Ahh, I could be a cop."

00:01:59.834 --> 00:02:02.100
-Yeah.
-Ehh, I could be a cop.

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:04.501
And so I'm a cop. I'm a cop!

00:02:04.501 --> 00:02:06.400
-Do you like it?
-Oh, I love it.

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:08.267
Well, first of all,
why do I like it?

00:02:08.267 --> 00:02:10.367
Because I don't have to
hold for laughs.

00:02:10.367 --> 00:02:12.067
I like that.

00:02:12.067 --> 00:02:15.667
I found out -- I was on
"Finding Your Roots,"

00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:18.234
which the show on PBS
with Henry Louis Gates.

00:02:18.234 --> 00:02:21.067
And I found out that
my great-grandfather

00:02:21.067 --> 00:02:23.033
was killed, was murdered.

00:02:23.033 --> 00:02:25.767
He and the nephew,
and you take a look at him --

00:02:25.767 --> 00:02:27.267
and this is something
I never knew --

00:02:27.267 --> 00:02:30.367
he could have been a gangster.
-Really?

00:02:30.367 --> 00:02:32.934
-What happened between
him and me?

00:02:32.934 --> 00:02:34.367
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.367 --> 00:02:35.767
Why aren't I tough?

00:02:35.767 --> 00:02:37.601
Why am I not a tough guy?

00:02:37.601 --> 00:02:39.734
-Well, it didn't seem like
it worked out great for him.

00:02:39.734 --> 00:02:42.834
-No, but let's hope
he deserved it.

00:02:42.834 --> 00:02:44.300
-Yeah, well, you know what?

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:45.601
That's a good way of
looking at it.

00:02:45.601 --> 00:02:48.801
-Yeah, I mean, he got murdered.

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:52.133
My grandfather was,
they called him an athlete

00:02:52.133 --> 00:02:54.367
because he had his nose broken
11 times.

00:02:54.367 --> 00:02:55.734
He was a boxer.

00:02:55.734 --> 00:02:58.501
-This is your grandfather?
-My grandfather, Alvin.

00:02:58.501 --> 00:03:01.067
What happened between
him and me?

00:03:01.067 --> 00:03:05.067
He was a tough guy.
11 times his nose was broken.

00:03:05.067 --> 00:03:08.067
I was in a bike accident with
my friend, Bruce Stern,

00:03:08.067 --> 00:03:09.367
when I was in first grade.

00:03:09.367 --> 00:03:11.701
I fell on the sidewalk.
I broke my nose.

00:03:11.701 --> 00:03:13.067
That's all I got for it.
-Really?

00:03:13.067 --> 00:03:14.434
-That's the toughest I've been.

00:03:14.434 --> 00:03:15.667
-And you haven't been on
a bike since.

00:03:15.667 --> 00:03:17.267
-Yeah, right. No. I have.

00:03:17.267 --> 00:03:18.667
But you know what was weird
that night?

00:03:18.667 --> 00:03:21.634
Because you stay up late,
everything broken.

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:23.901
I watched "The Untouchables"
that night,

00:03:23.901 --> 00:03:27.300
and Al Capone,
at the end of the show --

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:29.701
you know, the bad guy
always loses.

00:03:29.701 --> 00:03:31.267
-Yeah.
-It was a two-parter.

00:03:31.267 --> 00:03:32.934
But I don't know two-parters.

00:03:32.934 --> 00:03:35.501
I'd never seen an hour show,
much less "The Untouchables."

00:03:35.501 --> 00:03:38.968
Al Capone won.
To this day, I'm terrified.

00:03:38.968 --> 00:03:40.033
-Wow!

00:03:40.033 --> 00:03:41.300
-I was so scared
when I was a kid.

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:42.334
-Because you were a first
grader.

00:03:42.334 --> 00:03:43.734
You'd taken a bad fall
on the bike,

00:03:43.734 --> 00:03:45.033
and then you find out
the bad guy wins.

00:03:45.033 --> 00:03:46.167
-And you find out
the bad guys win.

00:03:46.167 --> 00:03:48.667
Eh, let's not talk about that.

00:03:48.667 --> 00:03:49.834
-I'm glad you managed to
work through that trauma.

00:03:49.834 --> 00:03:51.033
I want to ask,

00:03:51.033 --> 00:03:52.767
and then we're gonna take
a quick commercial break,

00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:54.634
but you've been in over
300 things.

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:56.367
We looked at your list
of credits.

00:03:56.367 --> 00:03:59.567
I would imagine there's a wide
breadth of people who come up

00:03:59.567 --> 00:04:01.667
to you and recognize you from
different shows and films.

00:04:01.667 --> 00:04:03.000
-They do.

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:06.467
If they're on the
East or West Coast,

00:04:06.467 --> 00:04:07.834
they come up for "Curb."

00:04:07.834 --> 00:04:10.300
If they're Jewish, it's a show
called "A Serious Man."

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:13.234
If they're of a certain age,
it's "Mad About You."

00:04:13.234 --> 00:04:16.033
The weird thing is "Big Mouth,"
you know.

00:04:16.033 --> 00:04:17.267
[ Cheers ]
Yes.

00:04:17.267 --> 00:04:18.734
-For the kids.

00:04:18.734 --> 00:04:23.400
-But it's also the people who
don't know me but do know me,

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:24.601
and they come up --

00:04:24.601 --> 00:04:26.467
I had one last night --

00:04:26.467 --> 00:04:30.000
I had one that's great
that came up last night.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.601
A guy goes, "Oh, dude!

00:04:31.601 --> 00:04:33.033
The last time I saw you

00:04:33.033 --> 00:04:35.567
was at Ringo Starr's 70th
birthday party

00:04:35.567 --> 00:04:37.167
at the Capitol Records
building."

00:04:37.167 --> 00:04:38.701
[ Laughter ]

00:04:38.701 --> 00:04:40.968
No. No.

00:04:40.968 --> 00:04:42.634
So he didn't know who I was.

00:04:42.634 --> 00:04:44.868
But the best, this is the best.

00:04:44.868 --> 00:04:47.567
"Oh, I don't --
Oh, yeah, I know!

00:04:47.567 --> 00:04:51.067
You used to run the porn stand
over on 34th Street."

00:04:51.067 --> 00:04:53.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:53.601 --> 00:04:55.434
-Now, Richard,

00:04:55.434 --> 00:04:57.701
were you around there enough

00:04:57.701 --> 00:04:59.534
that people thought you
maybe ran it?

00:04:59.534 --> 00:05:01.901
[ Laughter ]

00:05:01.901 --> 00:05:04.834
-So it matters where they're
from, what age they're from.

00:05:04.834 --> 00:05:07.300
Then they know. But I can't...

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:08.968
-You've got a lot of
other projects coming out.

00:05:08.968 --> 00:05:10.067
We're gonna talk abut them
real quick.

00:05:10.067 --> 00:05:11.300
We'll be right back
with Richard Kind.

